WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Think of the last real choice you made.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.700
Stay in, or go out.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.110
Say yes, or say no.

4
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.200
At that moment, both paths felt open.

5
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.490
The choice felt like yours.

6
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.860
The French philosopher
Jean-Paul Sartre went further.

7
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.390
Humans, he said, are condemned to be free.

8
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.760
But could you really
have chosen differently,

9
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.990
or does it only feel that way?

10
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.870
In this mission, you'll
meet libertarianism:

11
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.400
the view that at least some choices
are not fixed by prior causes.

12
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.930
Then you'll ask what each
view means for praise,

13
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.960
blame and punishment.

14
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.060
Your mission: weigh up whether you
really could have chosen differently,

15
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.190
or whether it only feels that way.
